Subject: Wifi: let the runner inhibit radio power-down

ndsrecomp modification to vendored melonDS src/Wifi.cpp (GPLv3 5(a)
notice; see patches/README.md for the convention).

UpdatePowerStatus asks the runner-owned nds_wifi_inhibit_power_down hook
before a power-down and, when it returns true, keeps the transceiver on
exactly as W_PowerDownCtrl bit 0 does. A DS MP host sleeps between beacons
and a station after its post-beacon window; the auth/assoc handshake
assumes replies within microseconds and fits in one wake window. Over a
link with real latency (the local wireless latency lab, later online play)
frames wait for the next wake-up and the join times out. The runner only
returns true when --local-wireless-stay-awake is on and the local MP
transport is open; otherwise behaviour is unchanged.

--- a/src/Wifi.cpp
+++ b/src/Wifi.cpp
@@ (runner hook declarations)
+bool nds_wifi_inhibit_power_down();
@@ Wifi::UpdatePowerStatus, after the W_PowerDownCtrl bit 0 check
+        if ((power == -1) && ::nds_wifi_inhibit_power_down())
+            power = 0;
